WEBVTT

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:04.173
Today, I'm going to talk about SELF-ASSESSMENTS.

00:00:04.193 --> 00:00:10.230
Everybody knows self-assessments is really important in terms of performance management.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:16.984
Basically, it's a piece of document that you officially present to your manager:

00:00:17.004 --> 00:00:20.195
what you have done in this performance cycle.

00:00:20.215 --> 00:00:24.165
However, a common mistake a lot of people make is:

00:00:24.185 --> 00:00:27.864
create a NEW STORY in their self-assessment,

00:00:27.614 --> 00:00:35.252
in the hope of your manager is going to actually DIG into the new story during the performance management cycle.

00:00:35.232 --> 00:00:36.852
It's not the best way.

00:00:36.872 --> 00:00:42.547
Because essentially, your manager is really trying to recall

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.877
their PERCEIVED REALITY during the whole cycle,

00:00:46.627 --> 00:00:53.396
even before your self-assessment landed in his or her desk.

00:00:53.416 --> 00:00:56.346
Essentially, you are trying to present information

00:00:56.096 --> 00:01:00.495
to MATCH with the reality that is already in your manager's mind.

00:01:00.515 --> 00:01:03.552
If you present something that is completely NEW —

00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:05.023
THAT IS A RISK.

00:01:05.043 --> 00:01:08.883
It's either: you've done something, but it's never in your manager's eye,

00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:11.451
or the impact is not in your manager's view —

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:12.666
which is a problem.

00:01:12.686 --> 00:01:17.767
Or you are fabricating something — which is even WORSE.

00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:25.186
So the best way to make sure your impact is really in your manager's mind is:

00:01:25.206 --> 00:01:30.926
during all of the ONE-ON-ONES across the whole performance management cycle —

00:01:30.676 --> 00:01:34.393
being six months, or being a whole year —

00:01:34.413 --> 00:01:38.673
using all the one-on-ones to present YOUR IMPACT,

00:01:38.423 --> 00:01:42.010
to present the DATA you changed,

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.296
to present the NEEDLE you moved.

00:01:44.316 --> 00:01:49.116
Only when you are doing those things, your manager will have

00:01:48.866 --> 00:01:54.240
a SHARED REALITY with you of what you have actually changed.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:59.180
And then your self-assessment will become a SUMMARY view

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.193
of what's already in your manager's head.

00:02:02.213 --> 00:02:08.253
And that is the best way to making sure your self-assessment LANDED in the right way.

00:02:08.273 --> 00:02:10.104
Hope this helps.
